{%- comment -%}
  PG Cart Mobile Price: the struck price, and the white band under checkout.

  ---------------------------------------------------- 1. THE STRUCK PRICE

  Three passes missed this because I was guessing at the markup. The line price
  is built by nc-linesave, and its own stylesheet names the parts:

      .nc-lsave            flex ROW, nowrap, gap 6px
      .nc-lsave-was        the struck compare-at
      .nc-lsave-now        the price charged
      .nc-lsave-off        the percentage pill

  So the struck figure is a <span class="nc-lsave-was">. It is NOT an <s>, a
  <del>, or the theme's .old-price -- and .old-price is a real element in the
  server markup, just hidden, which is what made it a convincing wrong answer.
  Every earlier rule here targeted those three and matched nothing.

  Because .nc-lsave is a nowrap row, was + now + pill cannot break, so when
  they are wider than the `pr` grid cell they overflow LEFT into `qt` -- the
  quantity stepper -- and the struck figure runs under the + button.

  Stacked into a column, ordered was / now / pill. No media query: what runs out
  of room is the DRAWER, about 380-420px wide on any device, so a viewport
  breakpoint never described the problem.

  ---------------------------------------------------- 2. THE WHITE BAND

  position:sticky with bottom:0 pins to the viewport only while the container
  is taller than the screen. On a short cart the panel sits at its natural
  place in the flow and the container's remaining height stays blank below it.
  Padding was never the cause. The pin is dropped on phones, so the panel ends
  where the content ends.

  Ordered after pg-cart-fast in footer-group, so this overrides the sticky rule
  that file sets, at equal specificity.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* ---- was above now, at every width ---- */
  #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave,
  #cart .l4ca > li section .nc-lsave,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave{
    display:flex !important;
    flex-direction:column !important;
    align-items:flex-end !important;
    justify-content:flex-end !important;
    flex-wrap:nowrap !important;
    gap:1px !important;
    max-width:100% !important;
    text-align:right !important;
  }
  #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave .nc-lsave-was,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave .nc-lsave-was{
    order:-1 !important;
    font-size:12px !important;
    line-height:1.15 !important;
    white-space:nowrap !important;
  }
  #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave .nc-lsave-now,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave .nc-lsave-now{
    order:0 !important;
    line-height:1.2 !important;
    white-space:nowrap !important;
  }
  #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave .nc-lsave-off,
  body.template-cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave .nc-lsave-off{
    order:1 !important;
    margin-top:2px !important;
  }

  /* the theme's own price node, on lines nc-linesave does not rewrite */
  #cart .l4ca > li .price.s1pr{
    display:flex !important;
    flex-direction:column !important;
    align-items:flex-end !important;
    gap:1px !important;
    text-align:right !important;
  }
  #cart .l4ca > li .price.s1pr .old-price{order:-1 !important}

  /* ---- no white band under the button ---- */
  @media (max-width: 600px){
    #cart .sticky-in-panel{
      position:static !important;
      bottom:auto !important;
      padding-bottom:calc(4px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)) !important;
      margin-bottom:0 !important;
    }
  }

  /* ---- the drawer disc, beaten on specificity ----
     pg-drawer writes #cart#cart#cart img.nc-dlogo and nc-recs writes
     display:block !important on the same element. A doubled id lost to the
     tripled one on any property they both set, so the disc could still paint
     on some breakpoints. Four ids ends the argument. */
  html body #cart#cart#cart#cart img.nc-dlogo{display:none !important}
</style>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Cart Mobile Price", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
